        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add experimental Claw package schema",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Adds the shared strict Claw v1 manifest schema, semantic validation, and safe derived summary.\n- Extends ClawHub storage contracts with `family: \"claw\"` and validated manifest metadata.\n- Keeps generic package publication closed to Claws; PR #3090 owns the first gated publication path.\n- Aligns the registry schema with the RFC sidecars for portable paths/avatars, exact packages, MCP declarations, cron declarations, and agent-owned fields.\n\nThis is ClawHub PR 1 of 4 for [OpenClaw RFC #27](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27).\n\n## Experimental boundary\n\nThis PR enables no Claw publication, search, detail, feed, or UI surface. Later surfaces require `CLAWHUB_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`; that deployment gate is not user consent and does not replace OpenClaw's plan-integrity confirmation.\n\nExisting generic publication continues to reject `family: \"claw\"`.\n\n## Contract alignment\n\nThe shared validator now enforces:\n\n- strict grouped schema with no unknown lifecycle fields;\n- NFC/case-folded workspace destination and hierarchy collision checks;\n- bounded image data URLs or managed workspace-relative avatar sidecars;\n- exact SemVer package coordinates keyed by `(kind, source, ref)`;\n- the Claw-specific heartbeat and human-delay allowlists;\n- mutually exclusive stdio/remote MCP shapes, unresolved env references, portable env keys, unique tool filters, immutable package-manager selections, and HTTPS/loopback URL policy;\n- explicit five-field cron expressions, required IANA timezone, `main|isolated` sessions, and exact delivery combinations.\n\nPublication and application still use their existing scanner, installer, scheduler, config, and consent owners; the schema does not create parallel runtime logic.\n\n## ClawHub stack\n\n1. **This PR:** schema ingestion and data model\n2. #3090: gated publication validation and authoring\n3. #3091: gated search, detail, and API projection\n4. #3092: hosted feed export and published lifecycle proof\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nEnvironment: WSL Ubuntu 24.04, current main merged into this branch.\n\nThe built `clawhub-schema` distribution was imported as a consumer alongside the real `convex/schema.ts`. A representative manifest with a managed local avatar validated and produced the expected safe summary; the Convex schema module loaded successfully. A second built-distribution invocation rejected `session: \"current\"` at `$.cronJobs.0.session`.\n\nNo reusable local Convex deployment was configured in the available worktrees, so this proof does not claim a live backend deployment. Convex schema/type/build integration is covered by the repository's real production build and type lanes below.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 23 focused Claw schema and package-label tests pass.\n- `bun run ci:types-build` passes, including schema, CLI/admin, Convex consumers, and production Vite/Nitro build.\n- `bun run ci:static` passes, including audit, generated-doc checks, formatting, type-aware lint, dead-code checks, and workflow pin validation.\n- built-distribution positive/negative consumer proof with `convex/schema.ts` passes.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- `codex review --base origin/main`: no actionable regression after fixing multi-package MCP pin validation.\n\n## Stack note\n\nThis remains a draft contract PR pending RFC/maintainer acceptance. Nothing in this stack should be merged out of order.",
